# ui_plus (UI Plus)

This is a reusable Flutter package, not an application.

**Positioning:** UI Plus — More power to your Flutter UI.

## Architecture

- Keep core APIs architecture agnostic.
- Do not depend on Bloc, Riverpod, Provider, GetX, Dio, or networking clients in the core package.
- Public APIs must be exported from `lib/ui_plus.dart`.
- Keep implementation files inside `lib/src/`.
- Do not ask package users to import from `src/`.

## Dependencies

- Do not add dependencies without explaining why they are needed.
- Prefer Flutter SDK APIs before introducing third-party packages.
- Do not add connectivity plugins to the core package. Built-in reachability uses
  a plugin-free probe (`PlusInternetChecker`); apps may still supply
  `bool` / `Stream<bool>` (custom wins).
- Optional state-management integrations belong in companion packages only when there is a real integration API.

## Quality bar

- Add widget tests for every new public component.
- Follow Dart formatting and Flutter lint rules (`very_good_analysis`).
- Use const constructors wherever appropriate.
- Respect Material 3, theme brightness, accessibility, and text scaling.
- Do not make breaking API changes without documenting the reason.
- Do not implement speculative features outside the current milestone.
- Run `dart format`, `flutter analyze`, and `flutter test` after changes.
- Update README and example usage when public APIs change.

## ScaffoldPlus

- `ScaffoldPlus<T>` is the primary all-in-one widget; it composes Flutter's native `Scaffold`.
- `PlusAsyncView` stays independently usable and must share the internal async renderer (`PlusAsyncBody`).
- Do not duplicate async state-switching logic between widgets.
- Keep `PlusLoader`, `PlusSkeleton`, `PlusEmptyState`, and `PlusErrorState` independently reusable.

## Milestones

- Source of truth: `plan.md` (Completed / In Progress / Planned / Future).
- v0.1–v0.6 shipped; **v1.0.0** is the stable API freeze. Post-1.0 work needs a
  written value case (or a new minor/major milestone in `plan.md`).
- Prefer multi-step app patterns over thin Material wrappers.
- Implement one component at a time with tests, example usage, and docs in the same task.
- Do not implement features outside the active milestone without explicit approval.
